map.Luhn 算法（又称\"模 10\"算法）由 IBM 科学家 Hans Pete:
The Luhn algorithm (also called the 'mod 10' algorithm) was proposed by IBM scientist Hans Peter Luhn in 1954, used to validate credit card numbers, IMEI, Canadian Social Insurance Numbers, etc.
      Steps:
      1. From right to left, multiply the even-position digits (2nd, 4th, 6th...) by 2;
      2. If the product is two digits, add the two digits (or subtract 9);
      3. Add all digits together;
      4. If the total is divisible by 10, validation passes.

